# h3 — MiniMax-H3 (Hailuo 3.0). NOT a chat model: video+audio generation.
# Text / first-frame in, MP4 with native stereo audio out (4-15 s, 24 fps).
#
# Different engine entirely: vLLM-Omni, not our dgx-spark-serve image. The
# recipe overrides IMAGE and launch-solo.sh does the rest — `rack up h3`
# works, `rack chat` and LiteLLM do not (the API is /v1/videos, multipart
# form in, MP4 out; nothing here speaks chat/completions).
#
# SOLO ONLY. vLLM-Omni has no multi-node story (every documented config is
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES on one host), so spark-2 sits this one out. It fits
# one Spark anyway, but only because of --quantization fp8:
#     DiT 66.3 GB bf16 -> ~33 GB fp8 at load (checkpoint stays bf16 on disk)
#     Qwen3-VL text encoder ~51.5 GB retained + video VAE 10.4 + audio VAE
#     ~= 95 GB resident vs 128 GB unified. Without fp8 it is 128+ GB of
#     weights and does not fit. Skip --enable-cpu-offload: fp8 wants to be
#     resident, and on unified memory "offload to CPU" frees nothing anyway.
#
# The checkpoint is GATED. Once per machine:
#   1. accept the license at https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3
#   2. put a token where the container mounts the cache:
#        printf '%s' 'hf_yourtoken' > ~/dgx/hf/token
# Then pull just the FL2VA partition (self-contained, 144 GB — the full repo
# is 498 GB; Ref2VA is a separate 144 GB partition and a separate server):
#   docker run --rm -v ~/dgx/hf:/root/.cache/huggingface \
#     --entrypoint bash vllm/vllm-omni:v0.26.0 -c \
#     "hf download MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3 --include 'FL2VA/*' \
#        --local-dir /root/.cache/huggingface/local/MiniMax-H3"
#
# Speed, honestly: MiniMax's reference numbers are 87 s per 8.7 s clip on
# FOUR B300s. One GB10 is a different weight class — expect tens of minutes
# per clip, first request slower still (regional torch.compile warmup).
# The levers, in order: duration, resolution, num_inference_steps (50 is
# reference; the upstream quality harness validates down to 10).
#
# Serving notes:
#   - port 8091, bound 127.0.0.1 by launch-solo.sh — reach it through the
#     hermes tunnel (18091), never open it on the LAN
#   - `rack status` polls :8888 so it will say "not answering"; instead:
#       curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8091/health   or   rack logs -f
#   - one generation request per diffusion batch; the console queues
#   - attention backend: leave unset. Platform default on sm_12x is
#     CUDNN_ATTN; the doc examples say FLASH_ATTN but that wraps FA4,
#     which targets datacenter Blackwell (sm_100/103), not GB10
# v0.26.0, NOT the minimax-h3 tag: that day-0 preview shipped vLLM-Omni
# 0.1.dev2381 against vLLM 0.26.0 and warned about it at startup — then
# proved it during fp8 load (H3's 2-arg fc1 weight loader called with 3 args
# by vLLM's online-quant layerwise reloader; signatures drifted between the
# packages). The v0.26.0 release (08-03) is the aligned build and lists
# MiniMax H3 (#5691) as a headline feature.
IMAGE=vllm/vllm-omni:v0.26.0
MODEL=/root/.cache/huggingface/local/MiniMax-H3/FL2VA
SERVE_ARGS=(
  --omni
  --port 8091                  # last flag wins over launch-solo's 8888
  --trust-remote-code
  --num-gpus 1
  --quantization fp8           # load-time DiT fp8 — the fit depends on it
  --vae-use-tiling             # decode in tiles; peak memory, not quality
)
ENV_EXTRA=(
  VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn
  VLLM_OMNI_VIDEO_SYNC_TIMEOUT=7200   # sync endpoint; the console uses async + polling anyway
)
# H3-aware fp8 merged upstream (#5737) three hours after v0.26.0 was cut, so
# no published image has it yet. The mod overlays the two patched files;
# delete it (and this line) at the first post-08-04 vllm-omni release.
MODS=(mods/h3-fp8-0.26)
